Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

kinect-senses interoperates with, and its build/setup process fetches, the
following third-party software. These components are NOT redistributed in this
repository — `setup.ps1` downloads or clones them at build time — and each
remains under its own license and copyright:

* libfreenect — The OpenKinect Project
    https://github.com/OpenKinect/libfreenect
    Dual-licensed under the Apache License 2.0 and the GNU GPL v2.0.
    A small patch in this repo (patches/libfreenect-mingw-sleep.patch) adds a
    POSIX sleep() shim to platform/windows/unistd.h so it builds with modern
    MinGW-w64 gcc. That patch is a derivative of libfreenect and is offered
    under the same terms as libfreenect.

* libusb — The libusb Project
    https://github.com/libusb/libusb
    Licensed under the GNU LGPL v2.1 or later.

* Zadig / libwdi — Pete Batard (Akeo Consulting)
    https://github.com/pbatard/libwdi
    Used (optionally, on demand) to install libusb-compatible USB drivers.
    Licensed under the GNU LGPL v3 or later.

